Title: THE GROOMSMEN'S GUIDE
Author: Marcus Webb
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


INT. TUXEDO SHOP - DAY

DAVE KIM picks identical tuxes. TOM and PETE argue about bow ties.
DAVE
Same cut, same color. Peace in our time.

INT. BRIDAL SHOP LOBBY - DAY

Dave waits with a smoothie. His fiancée MAYA texts: Do not buy anything stupid.
DAVE
Define stupid. Technically everything is stupid if you zoom out.

INT. STRIP MALL BAR - NIGHT

The guys drink. Dave reveals the MAGNETIC GUEST BOOK.
PETE
Your mother-in-law said no props. This is a prop with Wi-Fi.

INT. REHEARSAL DINNER - NIGHT

DIANE gives a polished toast. Tom's knee jabs Dave under the table.
DIANE
We want elegance. Not gadgets. Not chaos.

INT. HOTEL SUITE - NIGHT

Dave practices his speech in the mirror. The guest book hums on the desk.
TOM
Unplug it. Unplug your dreams. Save the marriage.

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - DAY

Florists everywhere. The guest book sticks to a rolling cart.
PETE
It's following us like a golden retriever with a screen.

INT. CHAPEL ANTEROOM - DAY

Dave adjusts his cufflinks. MAYA looks radiant, suspicious.
MAYA
You promised no surprises. Your face is doing surprise math.

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - NIGHT

First dance ends. Dave approaches the mic. Tom kills the lights by mistake.
TOM
Wrong switch! I swear on my toenail!

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - NIGHT

The guest book projects photos — including Tom's rehearsal toast.
DAVE
Maya, I wanted tonight to be perfect. Instead, you get us. All of us.

INT. HOTEL BALLROOM - NIGHT

Diane sighs, then laughs. Maya takes the mic from Dave.
MAYA
He bought one stupid thing. He married the right person. I'll allow it.

FADE OUT.


THE END
